{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1359844-fate-like-prime-effects-via-nimbus-manipulation","id":1359844,"title":"Fate-like Prime effects via Nimbus manipulation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-08T21:56:45-08:00","id":1359844,"title":"Fate-like Prime effects via Nimbus manipulation","content":"Nimbuses are an explicit purview of Prime and can thus be changed, guided, activated and empowered.<br /> <br /> By manipulating their short term nimbus, a mage can access various dice tricks. <br /> And by manipulating their long term nimbus a mage can cause various Fate-like narrative effects.<br /> <br /> Downsides include:<br /> -less finesse and direct control than actual Fate magic<br /> -being limited by the number of nimbuses available to manipulate<br /> -needing two to three spells to alter, empower, and activate a Nimbus to imitate a single Fate spell<br /> <br /> <br /> thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T22:36:44-08:00","id":1359846,"title":"","content":"Neither of these work.<br /> <br /> Your Long-Term Nimbus is literally &quot;you and things you have sympathetic connections with (to increasingly increasingly tenuous degrees as Wisdom drops) are more likely to be coincidentally entangled in magical shenanigans appropriate to your Path in a way that explicitly cannot be controlled.&quot;<br /> <br /> Your Immediate Nimbus affects <i>other people</i>, and not many of them at that outside the limited circumstance of a spell-free flare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T04:39:18-08:00","id":1359877,"title":"","content":"With spells that flare your Nimbus for you and increase its duration, it might be worth manipulating the effects, but they're generally lackluster (a small dice bonus/penalty, no dice tricks) and completely forgotten/ignored in play in my experience. You're often better off using Platonic Form (or whatever that spell is called) to gain a good tool.<br /> <br /> I don't recall whether the long term Nimbus is explicitly protected from all types of manipulation, but even if it wasn't you'd probably need to have the spell on you for quite some time before any effects start leaking out to your sympathetic connections, or include Space to directly affect your connections. Either way it's only going to change a slight tendency towards specific things and you'd have no guarantee that it'd ever happen to a specific sympathetic connection. Simply put, not worth it even if it's possible.<br /> <br /> Also, I think directly altering your Nimbus (as opposed to altering how it interacts with the world, such as Veiling its imprints, magnifying its effects, or even extending it to someone else as a second focal point) implies you're directly altering a part of yourself as a mage. I.e. template modification. Compare with Apocalypse, which grants your Active Mage Sight to the subject (i.e. transferring its effects), but you can't grant Mage Sight for Arcana you don't have and you can't change which ones counts as ruling. You can do a lot with it, but in the end you're fundamentally unable to alter the nature of your Mage Sight, and I think that should apply to Nimbuses as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T10:39:48-08:00","id":1359919,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> just as a point, Nimbus Tilts do add dice tricks &quot;A benefited Skill also gains the 8-Again quality. A penalized Skill loses the 10-Again quality.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2947-forgeeternal","name":"ForgeEternal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T10:43:44-08:00","id":1359921,"title":"","content":"The Nimbus can change as you increase in Gnosis, so I dunno, I think since it's mutable enough already I'd allow it to be altered from what it is. Altering and amplifying the Immediate Nimbus to give others specific dice tricks would be fine in my book.<br /> <br /> Altering your Nimbus would change what your LTN is doing, sort of, but it wouldn't change what it's affecting (Your sympathetic connections not shielded by Shadow Name). There's no way to direct it either. The LTN is like...well, it affects more connections the lower your Wisdom gets, and its generally going to do things that push you toward your Obsessions, Legacy and Shadow Name. They're essentially a mild version of the Tulpa generated by the Rapt. The Rapt have no control over their Tulpa, the Tulpa push them to follow their Fault. So altering your Nimbus might change how the LTN pushes you toward those things, but unless you also change those things it pushes you toward it'll keep on pretty much the same path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T13:01:24-08:00","id":1359948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1359844-fate-like-prime-effects-via-nimbus-manipulation?p=1359877#post1359877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With spells that flare your Nimbus for you and increase its duration, it might be worth manipulating the effects, but they're generally lackluster (a small dice bonus/penalty, no dice tricks) and completely forgotten/ignored in play in my experience. You're often better off using Platonic Form (or whatever that spell is called) to gain a good tool.<br /> <br /> I don't recall whether the long term Nimbus is explicitly protected from all types of manipulation, but even if it wasn't you'd probably need to have the spell on you for quite some time before any effects start leaking out to your sympathetic connections, or include Space to directly affect your connections. Either way it's only going to change a slight tendency towards specific things and you'd have no guarantee that it'd ever happen to a specific sympathetic connection. Simply put, not worth it even if it's possible.<br /> <br /> Also, I think directly altering your Nimbus (as opposed to altering how it interacts with the world, such as Veiling its imprints, magnifying its effects, or even extending it to someone else as a second focal point) implies you're directly altering a part of yourself as a mage. I.e. template modification. Compare with Apocalypse, which grants your Active Mage Sight to the subject (i.e. transferring its effects), but you can't grant Mage Sight for Arcana you don't have and you can't change which ones counts as ruling. You can do a lot with it, but in the end you're fundamentally unable to alter the nature of your Mage Sight, and I think that should apply to Nimbuses as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>The prime 2 spell Nimbus Forgery, from Signs of sorcery, can alter your nimbus emulating one you have already scrutinized","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T15:06:19-08:00","id":1359975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1359844-fate-like-prime-effects-via-nimbus-manipulation?p=1359948#post1359948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The prime 2 spell Nimbus Forgery, from Signs of sorcery, can alter your nimbus emulating one you have already scrutinized</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose the author and I had different ideas about the metaphysical significance of the Nimbus Tilt, as well as how far you can go with only Veiling. To me, using Prime Veiling to change the effects of a Nimbus Tilt is similar to using Life Veiling to disguise a Leg Wrack Tilt as an Arm Wrack Tilt to the point where the subject actually replaces the effects of them and can walk freely. Life could most certainly do that, but not through Veiling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 01-09-2020, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T15:16:24-08:00","id":1359980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1359844-fate-like-prime-effects-via-nimbus-manipulation?p=1359975#post1359975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose the author and I had different ideas about the metaphysical significance of the Nimbus Tilt, as well as how far you can go with only Veiling. To me, using Prime Veiling to change the effects of a Nimbus Tilt is similar to using Life Veiling to disguise a Leg Wrack Tilt as an Arm Wrack Tilt to the point where the subject actually replaces the effects of them and can walk freely. Life could most certainly do that, but not through Veiling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Following the practice logic i think that a level 4 patterning would be required, but i also think that a Prime spell should be able to alter the Nimbus so much","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T20:04:11-08:00","id":1360035,"title":"","content":"Nah, Weaving could switch you from leg wrack to arm wrack. You\u2019re moving the wrack around, not changing it completely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T23:10:30-08:00","id":1360070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1359844-fate-like-prime-effects-via-nimbus-manipulation?p=1360035#post1360035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, Weaving could switch you from leg wrack to arm wrack. You\u2019re moving the wrack around, not changing it completely.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that i think the Patterning practice would be required to alter this much the nimbus, i agree with you for the life spell","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T02:21:09-08:00","id":1360086,"title":"","content":"If the Nimbus Tilt isn't off limits, then I also think Weaving would be enough. You're changing one aspect of the subject, not transforming the whole of the subject. Especially the way that Nimbus Forgery is written where it only affects one of the three Nimbus parts without a Reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 01-10-2020, 06:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T08:56:10-08:00","id":1360131,"title":"","content":"Yup, what Tessie said, just Weaving to slap your Nimbus around like putty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T11:27:33-08:00","id":1360170,"title":"","content":"Do we think Weaving or Patterning to allow your Nimbus Tilt to affect you, too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T11:47:53-08:00","id":1360176,"title":"","content":"Since you're never affected by your Nimbus Tilt normally it's not Compelling, but Nimbus Tilts affecting people is how they usually work so it would be Ruling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-11T11:10:07-08:00","id":1360355,"title":"","content":"Narcissus' Mirror from SoS is a two dot spell that deflects Nimbus back on its creator. So I wager affecting yourself with your own Nimbus by deflecting it back onto you is an Apprentice level spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T01:47:26-08:00","id":1360475,"title":"","content":"Yeah, my thoughts when I was talking about needing three spells were:<br /> Prime 3 Weaving to alter the nimbus tilt + a reach to alter the long term nimbus + another reach if the new nimbus is not appropriate to the subject's Path and Legacy)<br /> Prime 1 or 2 for targeting the nimbus at an arbitrary person (including yourself)<br /> Prime 3 Perfecting to strengthen the long term nimbus into a dramatic RIGHT NOW effect (such as the Gauntlet cracking open around a Thyrsus just long enough for possessing spirits to dart through and start causing trouble. Or a 15 car pileup to happen in a circle around an Acanthus. Or for the Moros's new &quot;closed room murder mysteries keep happening wherever I go&quot; nimbus to kick into effect as gunfire is heard nearby)<br /> <br /> Though come to think of it, Patterning could probably handle all of that together as a single spell, since it's fundamentally rewriting the nature of &quot;what is a nimbus?&quot; from the ground up. I'd keep the reach cost to making a Nimbus that doesn't match the mage's Path/Legacy though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T05:14:43-08:00","id":1360502,"title":"","content":"It is interesting that Narcissus' Mirror is actually a Life and/or Mind spell depending on whether it affects Physical and/or Mental and Social traits respectively, while adding Prime allows the reflection of aura of other supernaturals. Perhaps Prime can also be used to affect all traits simultaneously, just like it can counterspell all other Arcana. This is kind of Prime's shtick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}